Description: ash: the fallbacks for an old libc, for Linux 2.6.16
 The libc (musl; before it, the old toolchain's glibc 2.8) defines
 F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC and O_CLOEXEC, but Linux 2.6.16 predates both (2.6.24 and
 2.6.23): fcntl(F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC) fails with EINVAL (glibc then failed with
 it, and ash couldn't run a script: "sh: 3: Invalid argument"; musl falls
 back to F_DUPFD), and O_CLOEXEC is ignored, so ash's own descriptors would
 leak into what it runs. ash has fallbacks for a libc without them
 (F_DUPFD, then FD_CLOEXEC); use those.
